/* en-id Compliments deck (writer C, added later). One card per line: target | pron | meaning | note. pron generated by tools/target/id/respell.js. */
module.exports = {
  "Compliments": `
Masakan Ibu enak sekali. | mah-SAH-kahn EE-boo EH-nahq suh-KAH-lee | Your cooking is delicious. (to an older woman) | To the host. To an older man: Masakan Bapak; to a friend: Masakan kamu. masakan = cooking, the dishes.
Ibu pintar masak, ya. | EE-boo PEEN-tahr MAH-sahq yah | You're a really good cook. (to an older woman) | pintar masak = good at cooking; ya at the end makes it warm. To a man: Bapak pintar masak, ya.
Bagus sekali! | BAH-goos suh-KAH-lee | Well done! | Literally "very good". Fine with anyone, any age. sekali goes after the adjective.
Wah, kamu jago! | wahh KAH-moo JAH-goh | Wow, you're really good at this! (to a friend) | jago = skilled, a friendly everyday word. To an older person: Wah, Bapak jago! or Wah, Ibu jago!
Ide bagus! | EE-deh BAH-goos | Good idea! | The noun comes first: ide bagus, never bagus ide. Fine with anyone.
Kamu baik sekali. | KAH-moo BAH-eeq suh-KAH-lee | You're so kind. (to a friend) | baik = kind here (also good, fine). To an older person: Bapak baik sekali or Ibu baik sekali.
Kamu lucu sekali! | KAH-moo LOO-choo suh-KAH-lee | You're so funny! (to a friend) | lucu = funny, and also cute: said of a baby, a pet or a thing it means cute.
Anak Ibu pintar sekali. | AH-nahq EE-boo PEEN-tahr suh-KAH-lee | Your child is very smart. (to a mother) | A warm, very common compliment to parents. To a father: Anak Bapak pintar sekali.
Rumah Ibu nyaman sekali. | ROO-mahh EE-boo NYAH-mahn suh-KAH-lee | Your home is so cozy. (to an older woman) | nyaman = comfortable, cozy: what a guest naturally says. To a man: Rumah Bapak nyaman sekali.
Kamu cocok pakai batik. | KAH-moo CHOH-chohq PAH-kai BAH-teeq | Batik looks great on you. (to a friend) | cocok = it suits you; pakai = wearing. To an older person: Bapak or Ibu cocok pakai batik.
Bahasa Indonesianya lancar sekali! | bah-HAH-sah een-doh-neh-see-AH-nyah LAHN-chahr suh-KAH-lee | Your Indonesian is really fluent! | You'll hear this often, even after a few words. -nya stands for "your", so no choice of "you" is needed.
Ah, biasa saja. | ahh bee-AH-sah SAH-jah | Oh, it's nothing special. | The usual reply to praise: Indonesians tend to play a compliment down, not simply accept it. Casual: Ah, biasa aja.
Belum lancar, masih belajar. | buh-LOOM LAHN-chahr MAH-seeh buh-LAH-jahr | Not fluent yet, I'm still learning. | The expected modest reply to praise for your Indonesian. Literally "not yet fluent, still learning".
Terima kasih atas pujiannya. | tuh-REE-mah KAH-seeh AH-tahs poo-jee-AHN-nyah | Thank you for the compliment. | Polite and a little formal. A plain Terima kasih with a smile is fine too; a modest line usually follows.
`
};
